  "reflectionText": "The fingers of a man's hand wrote on the wall beside the lampstand at the feast, and the joints of the king's hips were loosed. Daniel read it: numbered, weighed, divided. What is the courage of telling the king what the writing says, when the king is still drinking from the temple wine?"
